crossfont 0.8.0..0.9.0 on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6.8): src/darwin/mod.rs Font::get_glyph rasterizes into a bitmap context
created with a NULL data pointer and reads the pixels back with CGBitmapContextGetData; on 10.6 that returns NULL for a
Quartz-allocated bitmap (10.6 is the first release to accept NULL data at all) and `cg_context.data().to_vec()` copies from
address 0 (alacritty 0.17.0: EXC_BAD_ACCESS in __memcpy under ConvertVec::to_vec under Font::get_glyph, first glyph of
GlyphCache::load_font_metrics). On PowerPC the buffer is a Vec owned by the function and handed to CGBitmapContextCreate.

